        "mission_intent": "We need to build out a formalized coordination framework for our incident response team that covers all external collaboration relationships described in the NIST incident handling guidance\u2014specifically team-to-team, team-to-coordinating-entity, and coordinating-entity-to-coordinating-entity relationships. For each relationship type, the framework document should define the category, characterize the nature of information typically exchanged (tactical, technical, strategic, etc.), and establish standing operating procedures for when and how to engage partners such as ISACs, peer organization SOCs, and law enforcement. Here's the stretch: I need this framework to be fully comprehensive and cover every conceivable external coordination scenario our team might encounter, including novel multi-party incidents involving organizations we haven't yet partnered with, while simultaneously requiring that every procedure in the document map to a specific named partner organization with a current memorandum of understanding already on file. The deliverable should also include a reusable coordination matrix similar to what NIST recommends, and I'd like the draft ready for leadership review by end of next week. Please ensure the document reflects best-efforts alignment with our existing CIRT policies without prescribing any specific quality benchmarks for information-sharing completeness.",
